-# Freeze the vulnerability database into this immutable worker image. A new
-# worker image is the controlled database update unit; execution stays offline.
-# Existing release workflows provide a distinct value for each build attempt.
-ARG TRIVY_DATABASE_REFRESH=manual
-RUN test -n "$TRIVY_DATABASE_REFRESH" && setpriv --reuid=1000 --regid=1000 --init-groups \
-      env TRIVY_CACHE_DIR=/home/builder/.cache/trivy trivy image --download-db-only \
-    && setpriv --reuid=1000 --regid=1000 --init-groups \
-      env TRIVY_CACHE_DIR=/home/builder/.cache/trivy trivy image --download-java-db-only \
+# Database bytes are resolved only by the explicit update procedure. Build
+# retries consume identical OCI manifests/layers and never resolve mutable tags.
+COPY versions.json /app/versions.json
+COPY docker/trivy-databases.lock.json /app/docker/trivy-databases.lock.json
+COPY scripts/trivy-database-lock.mjs /app/scripts/trivy-database-lock.mjs
+RUN node /app/scripts/trivy-database-lock.mjs --install /home/builder/.cache/trivy "$(trivy --version | sed -n 's/^Version: //p')" \
+    && chown -R builder:builder /home/builder/.cache/trivy \
     && test -s /home/builder/.cache/trivy/db/trivy.db \
     && test -s /home/builder/.cache/trivy/java-db/trivy-java.db
 
diff --git a/docs/operations/local-image-vulnerability-scan.md b/docs/operations/local-image-vulnerability-scan.md
index c3188c1d..2d964fe7 100644
--- a/docs/operations/local-image-vulnerability-scan.md
+++ b/docs/operations/local-image-vulnerability-scan.md
@@ -73,11 +73,51 @@ deployment time. Operator-controlled runtime JSON can set all three
 Ages must be positive integers up to 30 days; size must be positive and at most
 32 GiB. Job configuration cannot waive this policy.
 
-Refresh by rebuilding the Buster image and completing the existing immutable
-image verification and release/promotion process before the source-age bound.
-The existing image workflows use a unique `TRIVY_DATABASE_REFRESH` build argument
-for every run and attempt. For a manual build, supply a unique value for that
-argument or disable the cached database layer. A reused image keeps aging, and
-an upstream stale snapshot still fails after rebuilding. No job downloads a new
-advisory database. `NextUpdate` is retained as scheduling evidence; a current
-`DownloadedAt` does not renew an old snapshot.
+Database inputs are authored in `versions.json` under `trivyDatabases` and
+generated into `docker/trivy-databases.lock.json` by `npm run versions:sync`.
+The Buster build verifies the selected scanner version, OCI manifest, compressed
+layer, extracted database and metadata bytes. It installs both databases together
+into a new cache. Builds consume immutable digests; rerunning a workflow or
+disabling its cache does not select newer advisory data.
+
+Before the source-age bound, explicitly select fresh inputs and rebuild:
+
+```sh
+mkdir -p dist/trivy-inputs
+node scripts/trivy-database-lock.mjs --resolve dist/trivy-inputs/update-20260921
+```
+
+Use a new directory name for every update. The resolver downloads both official
+GHCR database artifacts, verifies their bytes, and writes a proposed
+`trivy-databases.json` only after both pass. Review the preserved manifests,
+`db/metadata.json` and `java-db/metadata.json`, including upstream source dates.
+Copy the complete proposal object into `versions.json`'s `trivyDatabases` field,
+then run:
+
+```sh
+npm run versions:sync
+npm run versions:check
+node --test scripts/tests/trivy-database-lock.test.mjs
+```
+
+Review and commit the authored and generated lock together. Keep the resolver
+receipt and selected input identities with build evidence; downloaded database
+archives are large and do not belong in Git. Complete the immutable image
+verification, current scan, and release/promotion process before deployment.
+Schedule this update and promotion often enough to remain within the configured
+source-age policy, allowing for upstream publishing and build delays.
+
+An unavailable or mismatching object fails the build without a tag or mirror
+fallback. The installer rejects an existing cache and uses an exclusive sibling
+`CACHE.installing` directory. After an interrupted manual installation, confirm
+no installer still runs and remove only that attempt's abandoned guard and
+`.trivy-lock-*` staging directory before retrying into an absent cache. Normal
+Docker retries use a fresh failed layer. This publication guard is not a
+power-loss durability guarantee or a shared-cache garbage collector.
+
+A reused image keeps aging, and an upstream stale snapshot still fails after
+rebuilding. No job downloads a new advisory database. `NextUpdate` is retained
+as scheduling evidence; a current `DownloadedAt` does not renew an old snapshot.
+The loader preserves the original metadata bytes, including upstream's zero
+`DownloadedAt`. Trivy's offline mode accepts them; the runtime freshness gate
+continues to use `UpdatedAt`.
